@tradition rummage-day
// Rummage day: every fourth Sunday (week 4 of the cycle: days 28, 56, 84...), afternoon, the cargo hold on Deck 5.
// Main storage opens the old crates and lays out odd things nobody has claimed; take what's useful. Kept apart from the
// Sunday swap meet (mornings, the promenade) by deck and time; whatever nobody wants goes to the next swap meet.
// From day 1: the cycle also falls on day 0, your arrival afternoon, before you are aboard. No host: it's signed by Main storage. Needs the deck architect's places in the hold (event: 'rummage-day').
k: 459
title: Rummage day
when: every 4 weeks sunday week 4 from day 1
at: 14:00-15:45
min: 20
jitter: 25
where: 5 room Cargo hold: storage
where: 5 room Haulway: event
hold: none
who: shopper 70%, works 35%, everyone 18%
anim: talk
from: Main storage
ties: decor rummage-crates

== mail
- Rummage day tomorrow, {time}, the cargo hold. We're opening the old crates: spare parts, odd boots, a box of games nobody remembers loading. Take what's useful.

== ask
- Rummage day! Last time I found a perfectly good kettle.
- They're opening the old crates in the cargo hold this afternoon.
- I'm after a lamp. Or a hat. I'll know it when I see it.   #funny

== here
- What on earth is this?   #funny
- Who packed six left boots?   #funny
- Ooh. That's going on my shelf.

== thanks
- You dig through the old crates with the others and come away with something odd and lovely.   #warm

== chatter
- I found a whole box of chess pieces at rummage day. No board.   #funny
- Anything left from rummage day goes to the swap meet.
- The cargo hold smells of old crates and far-off places.   #warm
